      "lineNbr": 463,
      "author": {
        "id": 1347775
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-07T21:09:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason we can do this is that the HW power sequencing logic will ensure that the power on delay timing is met. So we just need to make sure the delay is longer than that. The reset won\u0027t de-assert until both the EC and power sequencing de-assert (ODL signal).\n\nWe could move the reset release to after the delay - we\u0027d need to add a 2nd delay after that for when we do the check to make sure the part is powered though since the reset will have a not-insignificant rising edge.\n\nLet me know if the comments I added are descriptive enough.",
      "parentUuid": "60ce7549_53d289ff",
      "revId": "706413d6db9e6c4a4b20bd803925a5ae8f939c81",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
